**Job Title** 




 Logistics Officer










**Job Scope** 




 The Logistics Officer is accountable for overseeing the inbound and outbound operations and inventory management. S/He maintains communication with carriers, suppliers, warehouses, custom brokers and others involved in the shipping and delivery of goods.










**Main Duties and Responsibilities** 




 Control the reception of merchandise to the warehouse and follow up on inventory levels and damaged goods if any; perform purchase transaction and share forwarder invoices with finance team.




 Manage outbound activities for customer orders;




 Manage outbound shipments, follow up with clearing and forwarding agents and monitor the turnaround time (TAT);




 Coordinate and arrange transportation of shipments to destination;




 Track shipments and update customers on a timely basis;




 Cooperate with the service and warehouse teams for smooth execution of shipments;




 Coordinate with clearing agents and customs to maximize efficiency in terms of time and quality;




 Verify customs documentations for exports and transfer of ownership;




 Manage the stock movement through the warehouse

